WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.200
ShiftLens watches your chatbot's answers and tells you when they change.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:28.200
It learns normal. A prompt change: no single answer crosses the line, the group does.

3
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.200
Live demo: Volt, a fictional support bot, has learned what normal looks like.

4
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.800
Its prompt changed to v2. One incident opened.

5
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:47.600
The note: what changed, probably why, and the requests that show it.

6
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.600
Each answer's distance from normal, with the threshold and the version change.

7
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.800
Ask about it. Every claim has to cite requests the agent actually found.

8
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.400
Answered in 4 s (wait cut). Click a request id to see that answer.

9
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:08.600
No code: paste or upload answers from before and after a change.

10
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:12.200
Same detection and investigation. About 40 s on the free server.

11
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:20.500
Done in 41 s (wait cut). The same kind of note, and nothing is stored.
